        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "697dc8d9-46d9-5069-a6a8-aeb41dae7f78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Danny Boyle, Irvine Welsh, Alex Garland, Andrew Macdonald\n- Works: Trainspotting, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Beach, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle, T2 Trainspotting, Porno, 28 Days Later\n- Roles: screenwriter, dramatist, director, producer, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge was born in 1964 and is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- Andrew Macdonald was born in 1966 and is a Scottish film producer.\n- John Hodge adapted Irvine Welsh's novel Trainspotting into the screenplay for the 1996 film Trainspotting.\n- John Hodge's film credits include Shallow Grave (1994), Trainspotting (1996), A Life Less Ordinary (1997), The Beach (2000), The Final Curtain (2002), and the short film Alien Love Triangle (2002).\n- The Beach is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle and adapted by John Hodge from Alex Garland's 1996 novel of the same name.\n- T2 Trainspotting was directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge, based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in the novels Trainspotting and Porno.\n- Andrew Macdonald is best known for collaborations with John Hodge and Danny Boyle, including Shallow Grave (1994), Trainspotting (1996), The Beach (2000), and 28 Days Later (2002).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
